 "summary": "MFI does not work as a dip-buying signal. On BTC, ETH and SOL, price moved the same after MFI(14) went below 20, or crossed back up through 20, as after a random candle. The result that holds up runs the other way: on daily candles, price kept rising after MFI(14) went above 80, and a short opened there did 10% worse than random after 20 days.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying the dip (below 20)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "No better than random entries on 1h, 4h or daily. This holds for the level below 20 and for the cross back up through 20."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting overbought (above 80)",
   "verdict": "worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on daily, and it holds without its strongest stretch. On 1h and 4h it also lands below the luck band, but there it rests on one stretch each."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the cross down through 80",
   "verdict": "fragile-worse",
   "text": "Below the luck band on 4h and daily, but only because of signals between Aug 27 and Aug 31, 2021 on 4h and between Aug 12 and Sep 13, 2021 on daily. Without them, it is chance."
  },
  {
   "use": "Riding momentum (crosses up 50)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "No different from random entries on 1h, 4h or daily."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the cross down through 70",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Inside the luck band on 1h, 4h and daily."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Going long while MFI(14) was below 20 on 1h gave 6,764 entries in 1,387 separate moves. Twenty candles later, they were 0.08% behind random entries, inside the luck band. The cross back up through 20 enters about a third as often and lands in the same place.",
  "Shorting while MFI(14) was above 80 did 10% worse than random entries after 20 days on daily. The result holds without its strongest stretch, between Aug 10 and Sep 12, 2021. It also shows at 10 candles, but not at 50 or 100. On BTC 1h the same short did 0.33% worse and held without its strongest stretch. Readings above 80 marked buying that continued, not tops.",
  "On 1h and 4h, the pooled short above 80 also fell below the band, by 0.24% and 1%. On 1h that came from signals on Aug 15–16, 2021, and on 4h from signals between Aug 27 and Sep 7, 2021. The cross down through 80 on 4h looked worse only because of 4 signals between Aug 27 and Aug 31, 2021. Leave those stretches out and all three land in chance.",
  "On BTC 4h, buying below 20 looked 1.36% worse than random. That came from 24 entries on May 7–11, 2022, during the Terra collapse, and without them it is chance. On daily, each coin has fewer than 30 episodes below 20, too few to judge on its own.",
  "Crosses up through 50 and down through 70 stayed inside the luck band on every timeframe. On 1h, MFI(14) crosses up 50 about four times as often as it crosses up 20, and price after those crosses moved the same as after random candles.",
  "For a long DCA bot, an MFI(14) dip condition adds nothing on these pairs, and the DCA orders and take profit do the work. MFI carries information above 80 on daily, where it marked strength that kept going. A short bot can treat daily MFI(14) above 80 as a reason to leave that entry out. A long bot can test it as a trend filter beside its other conditions."
 ],
